meta {
  name: Add a wishlist entry
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/wishlist
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Silksong",
    "system": "",
    "genres": [],
    "releaseDate": null,
    "imageUrl": "",
    "igdbId": null,
    "starred": true,
    "notes": "day one",
    "dateAdded": "2026-08-18"
  }
}

docs {
  Same IGDB-pick-or-manual shape as adding a game, but only `name` is required:
  the wishlist dedupes by name alone and `system` may stay undecided.

  `dateAdded` defaults to the SERVER clock, which is UTC in production, so an
  evening write in a western timezone would land on the wrong day. The web UI
  always sends the browser-local date explicitly; the default exists for tests
  and hand-rolled calls like this one.

  - 201 created
  - 403 not onboarded
  - 409 that name is already wishlisted
  - 422 blank name, non-IGDB imageUrl
  - 429 over the write budget
}
